<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qays</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qays were the northern Arab tribal grouping that opposed the Yemeni or Qahtani faction in the early Islamic period. Their rivalry dominated the politics and armies of the late Umayyad period. The site's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> profile identifies it as a cause of the paralysis that preceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s fall in 750.</p></div>
